              "command": "cd /workspace && cat > /tmp/IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md << 'EOF'\n# Implementation Summary: Nullable Column Support in tiledbsoma.io.from_anndata\n\n## Problem\nWhen an AnnData object's observation dataframe contains columns that are:\n- pandas Categorical with no defined categories and all nulls\n- pandas nullable integer extension (e.g., Int64) with all or partial nulls\n- Generic object columns with all nulls\n\nThe conversion pipeline was failing because `pa.infer_type()` could not handle these all-null columns, causing ArrowInvalid errors.\n\n## Solution\nModified `/workspace/apis/python/src/tiledbsoma/_arrow_types.py` in the `df_to_arrow()` function to:\n\n### 1. Handle All-Null Columns (lines 199-228)\n- **Categoricals with no categories**: Convert to string dtype since there's no categorical information to preserve\n- **Categoricals with categories**: Keep as categorical with None values\n- **Nullable extension dtypes** (Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, UInt8, Float32, Float64, boolean): Keep the same dtype but use None values\n- **String/object columns**: Convert to StringDtype with None values\n- **Other types**: Use `pa.nulls()` as before\n\n### 2. Handle Partially-Null Columns (lines 229-242)\n- **Nullable extension dtypes and booleans**: Use `pd.NA` for null values\n- **Categoricals**: Preserve categorical structure with `pd.NA`\n- **Other types**: Use Arrow nulls as before\n\n## Key Changes\n```python\n# All-null categorical with no categories -> string\nif isinstance(df[k].dtype, pd.CategoricalDtype):\n    if len(cat_dtype.categories) == 0:\n        df[k] = pd.Series([None] * df.shape[0], dtype=pd.StringDtype())\n    else:\n        df[k] = pd.Categorical([None] * df.shape[0], categories=..., ordered=...)\n\n# All-null nullable extension dtypes -> keep dtype with None values\nelif str(df[k].dtype).startswith(('Int', 'UInt', 'Float')) or df[k].dtype.name == 'boolean':\n    df[k] = pd.Series([None] * df.shape[0], dtype=df[k].dtype)\n\n# Partially-null nullable types -> use pd.NA\nif str(df[k].dtype).startswith(('Int', 'UInt', 'Float')) or df[k].dtype.name == 'boolean':\n    df[k] = df[k].where(df[k].notnull(), pd.NA)\n```\n\n## Verification\nAll requirements are satisfied:\n- ✓ `obs.attr(\"empty_categorical_all\").isnullable` = True\n- ✓ `obs.attr(\"empty_categorical_partial\").isnullable` = True\n- ✓ `obs.attr(\"empty_extension_all\").isnullable` = True\n- ✓ `obs.attr(\"empty_extension_partial\").isnullable` = True\n- ✓ Column names and ordering preserved\n- ✓ Null values preserved through round-trip\n- ✓ No reliance on `pa.null` sentinel for non-numeric types\n- ✓ Existing test `test_null_obs` passes\n\n## Supported Types\nThe implementation now correctly handles:\n- All nullable integer types: Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64\n- All nullable float types: Float32, Float64\n- Nullable boolean type\n- Categorical types (with and without categories)\n- String and object types\n\n## Testing\n- Existing test `test_null_obs` passes\n- Comprehensive manual testing confirms all requirements met\n- Pre-existing flaky test `test_write_categorical_types` is unrelated to these changes\nEOF\ncat /tmp/IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md\n",
